    markdown:
      "## create\n\n`client.robotsPreview.jobs.askQuestions.create(parameters: { asset_id: string; questions: object[]; language_code?: string; max_free_form_answer_length?: number; }, passthrough?: string): { id: string; created_at: number; parameters: ask_questions_job_parameters; status: job_status; units_consumed: number; updated_at: number; workflow: 'ask-questions'; errors?: job_error[]; outputs?: ask_questions_job_outputs; passthrough?: string; resources?: object; }`\n\n**post** `/robots/v0/jobs/ask-questions`\n\nCreates a new job that uses AI to answer questions about a Mux Video asset.\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `parameters: { asset_id: string; questions: { question: string; answer_options?: string[]; free_form_reply?: boolean; }[]; language_code?: string; max_free_form_answer_length?: number; }`\n  - `asset_id: string`\n    The Mux asset ID of the video to analyze.\n  - `questions: { question: string; answer_options?: string[]; free_form_reply?: boolean; }[]`\n    One or more questions to ask about the video. Each question can either select from answer_options (defaults to yes/no) or, by setting free_form_reply: true, receive a free-form prose answer.\n  - `language_code?: string`\n    BCP 47 language code of the caption track to analyze (e.g. \"en\", \"fr\"). When omitted, the SDK uses the default track.\n  - `max_free_form_answer_length?: number`\n    Experimental. Max character length for free-form answers. Ignored unless at least one question sets free_form_reply: true.\n\n- `passthrough?: string`\n  Arbitrary string stored with the job and returned in responses. Useful for correlating jobs with your own systems.\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ id: string; created_at: number; parameters: { asset_id: string; questions: object[]; language_code?: string; max_free_form_answer_length?: number; }; status: 'pending' | 'processing' | 'completed' | 'errored' | 'cancelled'; units_consumed: number; updated_at: number; workflow: 'ask-questions'; errors?: { message: string; type: string; retryable?: boolean; }[]; outputs?: { answers: object[]; }; passthrough?: string; resources?: { assets: { id: string; _links: object; meta?: object; passthrough?: string; }[]; }; }`\n\n  - `id: string`\n  - `created_at: number`\n  - `parameters: { asset_id: string; questions: { question: string; answer_options?: string[]; free_form_reply?: boolean; }[]; language_code?: string; max_free_form_answer_length?: number; }`\n  - `status: 'pending' | 'processing' | 'completed' | 'errored' | 'cancelled'`\n  - `units_consumed: number`\n  - `updated_at: number`\n  - `workflow: 'ask-questions'`\n  - `errors?: { message: string; type: string; retryable?: boolean; }[]`\n  - `outputs?: { answers: { answer: string; confidence: number; question: string; reasoning: string; skipped: boolean; }[]; }`\n  - `passthrough?: string`\n  - `resources?: { assets: { id: string; _links: { self: { href: string; }; }; meta?: { creator_id?: string; external_id?: string; title?: string; }; passthrough?: string; }[]; }`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport Mux from '@mux/mux-node';\n\nconst client = new Mux();\n\nconst askQuestionsJob = await client.robotsPreview.jobs.askQuestions.create({ parameters: { asset_id: 'mux_asset_123abc', questions: [{ question: 'Is this video about glasses?' }, { question: 'What is the primary subject?' }, { question: 'Describe the primary subject in one sentence.' }] } });\n\nconsole.log(askQuestionsJob);\n```",
